      <h2><a href="/future-self/">Fear of the future</a></h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <p>Everything we do to secure ourselves, every decision we make out of fear of the future, ends up destroying us, ends up making our future a little more bleak — the closer we are to the public ideal of “success”, the farther we go from our own private, ideal, from our soul, if you want…</p>

<p>Because ultimately it is not the future, but our <em>past</em> that defines us. The past determines who we are and it is the past that we should think about when making decisions, not the future. “What would my position be tomorrow?” is unimportant. But “How would I feel about <em>myself</em> tomorrow?” is the real question.</p>

<p>And you won’t feel good, if you are betraying your past self, for the welfare of a future self, which will never materialize, which remains only a vain hope, that gets more and more disconnected from reality.</p>

      </div>

    </article>

    
      <h2><a href="/prison/">My life is like a Prison</a></h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <p>“My life is like a prison”</p>

<p>I wrote this in my personal website when I was 14.</p>

<p>I was quite correct in pinpointing the problem, pinpointing how I, and many other people, felt, but I was off at identifying the cause — I thought, that I was kept in this prison by systems of power, like school, parents, later bosses and landlords. So I fought those.</p>

<p>But, after advancing with this fight, I realized that it is not the systems of power per se that limit me (although they are certainly designed to do that, and certainly help) but rather my engagement with those systems — fighting your parents, bosses etc. would just make you more like them. So, advance to the next stage, cancel them, stop engaging. Don’t break free, just walk away.</p>

<p>The systems of power are only holding your material self, divorce from it and you are free. Moreover, this is the only way to be free, otherwise you are just moving into a bigger cell.</p>

<p>As for the people, don’t hate them, don’t pity them, rather be compassionate and empathetic towards them, if possible, educate them over what they are doing!</p>

      </div>

    </article>

    
